 "result": "Added `src/utils/fetchWithTimeout.ts` and switched `src/routes/v2/billingExport.ts` to use it. Nothing has been run or type-checked.\n\n- **Wrapper:** `fetchWithTimeout(url, { method?, token?, body? })` enforces the 8000 ms timeout and formats the auth header as `Bearer <token>`. It also exports `FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS`.\n- **Billing route:** `loadInvoice` now calls `${BILLING_SERVICE_URL}/invoices/:id` with the caller's token, replacing the stub. A 404 from that service becomes a 404 response, and any other failure throws.\n- **Default URL:** `BILLING_SERVICE_URL` defaults to `http://localhost:8089`, which is the local daemon port and may not be where your billing service actually runs.\n- **Not migrated:** `auth.ts` and `dashboardApi.ts` still use their own inline timeouts. Say if you want them moved onto the wrapper.",
